    Correctly apply the end-of-contents octets to the right level (#134)
    
    Motivation
    
    In #125 we attempted to apply a hardening fix that would avoid allowing
    truncation of BER content by applying an end-of-contents octets at the
    wrong parse depth to a higher-level object. This fix was incomplete.
    
    Modifications
    
    Re-write the code to handle the end-of-contents octets as part of the
    loop instead of attempting to detect it after the fact. Add
    defense-in-depth for unexpected nodes.
    
    Results
    
    More robust against issues with end-of-contents octets.

